<rml>
<head>
	<title>Duel spectator frame (CDuelWatchMainFrameWindow)</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="base.rcss"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="duel_watch_frame.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="duel_watch_frame">
	<!-- The spectator's duel frame (CDuelWatchMainFrameWindow), in the main frame's place while the
	     duel-watch buff is on: the frame (menu_pk_01..03, 640 x 51 at the bottom) and the exit
	     button always; for a watched channel also the fighters' health and shield gauges (each
	     with its catch-up effect bar while it moves), their score marks and their names. A
	     LayoutMode::Hud window, so .screen is the 640x480 reference screen stretched W/640 x H/480
	     like the original; the names take their native size and cancel the stretch. Only the
	     exit button takes pointer events: its click is queued with duel_watch_exit, C++ keeps its
	     tooltip and sends the channel quit request. -->
	<div class="screen" data-style-transform="'scale(' + scale_x + ', ' + scale_y + ')'">
		<div id="back1"></div>
		<div id="back2"></div>
		<div id="back3"></div>
		<div id="fight" data-if="watching">
			<img class="gauge" data-for="g : gauges" data-attr-src="g.src" data-attr-rect="g.rect"
			     data-class-mirrored="g.mirrored" data-style-left="g.left + 'px'" data-style-top="g.top + 'px'"
			     data-style-width="g.width + 'px'" data-style-height="g.height + 'px'"/>
			<div class="score" data-for="left : score_marks" data-style-left="left + 'px'"></div>
			<span class="name" id="name_hero" data-style-font-size="hero_name.text_px + 'px'"
			      data-style-width="(55 * scale_x) + 'px'"
			      data-style-transform="'scale(' + inverse_scale_x + ', ' + inverse_scale_y + ')'">{{hero_name.text}}</span>
			<span class="name" id="name_enemy" data-style-font-size="enemy_name.text_px + 'px'"
			      data-style-width="(55 * scale_x) + 'px'"
			      data-style-transform="'scale(' + inverse_scale_x + ', ' + inverse_scale_y + ')'">{{enemy_name.text}}</span>
		</div>
		<div id="exit" data-event-click="duel_watch_exit"></div>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
